{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>Passive listeners and cancelling stale frames</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Always add <code>{ passive: true }</code> when you register a scroll listener that never calls <code>preventDefault()</code>. It tells the browser it can start scrolling immediately instead of waiting to see if your handler blocks it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Cancel any pending rAF handle when the component unmounts or the listener is removed, using <code>cancelAnimationFrame</code>, otherwise a queued frame can run its callback against DOM nodes that are already gone.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      For scroll-linked animation (parallax, progress bars tied to scroll position), read layout values like <code>scrollY</code> inside the rAF callback, not inside the raw scroll handler, to avoid forcing a synchronous layout read at a moment the browser hasn't finished its own scroll-position bookkeeping yet.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

