<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">
    Don't do real work inside a raw scroll handler. Set a flag, and do the work once per animation frame instead.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-mid">
    The tick-flag plus requestAnimationFrame pattern coalesces any number of scroll events between frames into a single update.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-staff">
    Always add passive: true to scroll listeners that never call preventDefault, and cancel any pending animation frame on cleanup.
  </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
